{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The problem does not contain a sure outcome (i.e., no 100% probability outcome), so the reference value is zero. The relevant information for the decision reason is the difference between each outcome and the reference value (which, in this case, equals the outcomes themselves, since the reference is zero), weighted by their probabilities. For Lottery A: (4000 - 0) × 0.25 = 1000, (2000 - 0) × 0.25 = 500, (0 - 0) × 0.5 = 0; total mean difference = 1500. For Lottery B: (6000 - 0) × 0.25 = 1500, (0 - 0) × 0.75 = 0; total mean difference = 1500. The mean differences are equal, so the reason would be indifferent between A and B.",
